      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I also think the actual game updates that go live should have \"patch notes\" mentioned in the \"Help and Info\" section of the main menu.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-11-21T14:22:18.173Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "# Dev updates ingame\nOver time I have noticed a large portion of the community don't actually view or are aware of dev updates, I feel like Vrchat should have better communication with the wider community rather than the just Vr fanatics.\nTo find info on the dev updates you have to go onto multiple platforms eg. Twitter, discord, Vrchat blogs.\nAndroid users really have to go out of their way to view these updates which most users on that platform don't.\n# Solution\nIn the new main menu update a new section to the menu was added called Help and Info. I feel that it would be amazing place to add dev updates into this section.\nAdditionally every Thursday/ Friday you can put the dev update notification in the quick menu bar and have it link to the dev update in the help and info section.\n# Conclusion\nThis hopefully will make Vrchat a more transparent platform and will allow users easily find the info.",
